### Describe the bug

If a local resolver is enabled on a NixOS host, NixOS containers fail to make use of it for dns resolution. The container `/etc/resolv.conf` point to localhost (the same as host):

```
[root@container:~]# cat /etc/resolv.conf 
# Generated by resolvconf
nameserver 127.0.0.1
nameserver ::1
options edns0 trust-ad
options edns0
```

However, this doesn't forward dns requests to the host.

It is possible to make dns resolution work in the container by also enabling a local resolver in the container config (e.g. `containers.container.config.services.kresd.enable = true;`).

### Steps To Reproduce
1. Set up a local resolver on the host:
```
  services.kresd.enable = true;
```

2. Set up a container with NAT networking:
``` 
config.networking.nat = {
    enable = true;
    internalInterfaces = ["ve-+"];
    externalInterface = config.local.webInterface;
    # Lazy IPv6 connectivity for the container
    enableIPv6 = true;
  };
};
containers.test = {
  autoStart = true;
  privateNetwork = true;
  localAddress = "192.168.102.1";
  hostAddress = "192.168.102.2";
  localAddress6 = "fc00::102:1";
  hostAddress6 = "fc00::102:2";
  config = {
    environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [ neovim ];
    system.stateVersion = "24.11";
  };
};
```

3. Enter the container, `sudo nixos-container root-login test`
4. `ping www.nixos.org`

### Expected behavior
DNS resolution should work in the container.

### Metadata
Please run `nix-shell -p nix-info --run "nix-info -m"` and paste the result.

```console
[user@system:~]$ nix-shell -p nix-info --run "nix-info -m"
 - system: `"x86_64-linux"`
 - host os: `Linux 6.10.5, NixOS, 24.11 (Vicuna), 24.11.20240919.d2151e9`
 - multi-user?: `yes`
 - sandbox: `yes`
 - version: `nix-env (Nix) 2.18.5`
 - nixpkgs: `/nix/store/swd656ypk2hhk88vhc510c5zz794778j-source`
```

